      "title": "Baptism, the Spirit, and Simon",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "block_2",
          "text": "The Samaritan episode deliberately distinguishes baptism from the later prayer and laying on of hands by Peter and John. Simon then tries to purchase the authority he sees associated with this action, and Peter sharply rejects the attempt. Readers differ over how this scene relates to other accounts of receiving the Spirit, so it is best not to force it into a single universal sequence.",
