      "title": "Isaiah and the Ethiopian Official",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "block_4",
          "text": "The passage the official reads belongs to Isaiah\u2019s portrayal of a servant who is humiliated, suffers and dies, bears on behalf of others, and is vindicated. Isaiah does not explicitly name this servant, and collective, individual, prophetic, messianic, and Christian readings have long been offered. Acts narrates Philip beginning with this text and explaining Jesus to the official.",
